;; The type of a LIDO subject (subject/@lido:type), after the LIDO 1.1
;; subjectWrap documentation: a subject is a description or identification of
;; what the work depicts ("ofness"), or an interpretation of its meaning
;; ("aboutness"). The LIDO Terminology's codes for these types are not listed:
;; they could not be checked offline, and a code is not guessed. Since lot
;; N7's review, the codes of the LIDO Terminology the review named are:
;; lido00525 Description, lido00136 Identification, lido00524 Interpretation,
;; and lido00745 Iconclass notation (a notation of what an image shows: of
;; ofness); a LIDO 1.0 `…/subject_type/<name>` URI is read by its name.
{:id     :lido/subject-types
 :source "LIDO 1.1 schema, subjectWrap (lido-schema.org, CC BY 4.0)"
 :concepts
 {:subject/ofness
  {:doc   "What is depicted: generic content (description) or a named subject (identification)."
   :terms ["description" "identification" "beschreibung" "identifizierung" "identifikation"]
   :patterns ["^https?://terminology\\.lido-schema\\.org/(?:lido00525|lido00136|lido00745)$"
              "^https?://terminology\\.lido-schema\\.org/subject_type/(?:description|identification|iconclass_notation)$"]}
  :subject/aboutness
  {:doc   "What the work means: its iconographical, thematic or symbolic interpretation."
   :terms ["interpretation" "deutung" "interprétation"]
   :patterns ["^https?://terminology\\.lido-schema\\.org/lido00524$"
              "^https?://terminology\\.lido-schema\\.org/subject_type/interpretation$"]}}}
